 0px\">http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier:type</td><td style=\"border-left-width: 0px\"/><td>Element `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.type` is part of an existing definition because parent element `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.type` has a context of DeviceDefinition based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `DeviceDefinition`.\nElement `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.type` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-right-width: 0px\">DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.deviceIdentifier</td><td style=\"border-left-width: 0px\">deviceIdentifier</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td style=\"border-right-width: 0px\">http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier:deviceIdentifier</td><td style=\"border-left-width: 0px\"/><td>Element `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.deviceIdentifier` is part of an existing definition because parent element `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.deviceIdentifier` has a context of DeviceDefinition based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `DeviceDefinition`.\nElement `DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.deviceIdentifier` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-right-width: 0px\">DeviceDefinition.regulatoryIdentifier.issuer</td><td style=\"border-left-width: 0px\">issuer</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td style=\"border-right-width: 0px\"